# a note of an operation that stays closed says which operation of the finished code made the value it hangs on, where the type of that value is not proven: the entry of the function, a call by value, a call of a function that is known, a read of a variable. A value that is read out of another value by a read that stays closed is no more proven than that value, so the note says what made that one: `holder.inner.a` and `value.a + 1` hang on the parameter. The cause that a report names comes from that, and from the kind of the operation for a call by value alone
# OPTIONS: report=Flow
# RUN: notes f2 f3 f4 f5 mechanisms=all
# CHECK: notes of f2:Body
# CHECK-NEXT: GenericOperation @86 in f2 from=EntryOfFunction cause=UnprovenEntryValue
# CHECK: notes of f3:Body
# CHECK-NEXT: GenericOperation @135 in f3 from=NotSaid cause=UnknownCallee
# CHECK-NEXT: GenericOperation @140 in f3 from=ResultOfCallByValue cause=ResultOfUnknownCallee
# CHECK: notes of f4:Body
# CHECK-NEXT: GenericOperation @189 in f4 from=EntryOfFunction cause=UnprovenEntryValue
# CHECK-NEXT: GenericOperation @196 in f4 from=EntryOfFunction cause=UnprovenEntryValue
# CHECK: notes of f5:Body
# CHECK-NEXT: GenericOperation @243 in f5 from=EntryOfFunction cause=UnprovenEntryValue
# CHECK-NEXT: GenericOperation @253 in f5 from=EntryOfFunction cause=UnprovenEntryValue
# where a join brings values of two kinds together, the result of a call and what a property held, the note says nothing of the value, and the report has no cause to name
# RUN(JOIN): notes f6 mechanisms=all
# JOIN: notes of f6:Body
# JOIN: GenericOperation @364 in f6 from=NotSaid cause=Unknown
# `countDown` calls itself, so no copy of it stands in line: what it gives to `ofCall` is the result of a call of a function that is known
# RUN(CALL): notes f7 mechanisms=all
# CALL: notes of f7:Body
# CALL-NEXT: GenericOperation @529 in f7 from=ResultOfDirectCall cause=UnprovenResultOfCall
# the variable of the loop is a join of what the entry brings and of what is read out of the variable itself. The edge that comes back to the join says nothing of its own, so the join says what the entry says
# RUN(LOOP): notes f8 mechanisms=all
# LOOP: notes of f8:Body
# LOOP-NEXT: GenericOperation @583 in f8 from=EntryOfFunction cause=UnprovenEntryValue
# LOOP-NEXT: GenericOperation @603 in f8 from=EntryOfFunction cause=UnprovenEntryValue
# a read of a variable is a resolved one: what it gives is what the variable holds, and nothing proves the type of that
# RUN(VARIABLE): notes f9 mechanisms=all
# VARIABLE: notes of f9:Body
# VARIABLE-NEXT: GenericOperation @664 in f9 from=PropertyOrVariable cause=UnprovenStoredValue
# the store into `globalThis.keep` asks an object without a layout for a property by its name: the types of its operands are proven
# RUN(BUILTIN): notes f0 mechanisms=all
# BUILTIN: GenericOperation @676 in f0 from=NotSaid asks=PropertyOfObjectWithoutLayout cause=NonLayoutObject
# let saved: any = (globalThis as any).saved;
# function ofParameter(value: any) { return value.a; }
# function ofResult(make: any) { return make().a; }
# function ofProperty(holder: any) { return holder.inner.a; }
# function ofSum(value: any) { return value.a + 1; }
# function ofEither(flag: any, make: any, holder: any) { const value = flag ? make() : holder.inner; return value.a; }
# function countDown(value: any, n: number): any { return n > 0 ? countDown(value, n - 1) : value; }
# function ofCall(value: any) { return countDown(value, 2).a; }
# function ofLoop(node: any) { let n = 0; while (node.next) { node = node.next; n++; } return n; }
# function ofVariable() { return saved.a; }
# (globalThis as any).keep = [ofParameter, ofResult, ofProperty, ofSum, ofEither, countDown, ofCall, ofLoop, ofVariable];

